  "body": "Chrome would like to limit the usage of `window.open()`, and we believe that there is rarely a valid purpose for that function when a page is exiting. We propose here a model for limiting `window.open()` similar to mechanisms already in place for modal dialogs like `alert()`, `confirm()`, and `prompt()` with [event loop](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop)'s [termination nesting level](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop), which additionally prevents the unloaded page to use a `window.open()` in another synchronously accessible windows.\n\nHowever, one difference between the proposed algorithm and the modal dialog functions is that the early return is mandatory unlike the returns in those functions. We have a strong preference to do that, as it allows testing through WPTs for browser interoperability.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/12577\n\n/cc @avidrissman, who has [already implemented](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/1180296) this change in Chromium.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3960/window-object.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 25, 2018, 4:21 PM GMT (c539ded)\">/window-object.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3960/825ede5...c539ded/window-object.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 25, 2018, 4:21 PM GMT (c539ded)\">diff</a> )",
